                            Preamble

  The GNU Affero General Public License is a free software licence,
with additional features to support the use of software on computer
networks.  If you can implement it as a conventional copyright-based
free software licence, that is preferable.  However, developers must
also be encouraged to implement these licences in software that runs
on server-side and other non-GUI applications where the user does not
typically receive a copy of its source code.

  Therefore the GNU Affero General Public License has two important
features: (1) it covers non-charting as well as charting distribution,
and (2) it has a clause which requires licensed code used in the
operation of a computer network to be made available as source code,
even if users do not receive a copy of it.

  The GNU Affero General Public License is licensed under the following
terms:

